cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LipidXplorer, please cite the preferred-citation below. The
  additional references under `references` describe later versions of the
  software and may be cited alongside it.
title: LipidXplorer
abstract: >-
  LipidXplorer supports bottom-up and top-down shotgun lipidomics experiments
  performed on all types of tandem mass spectrometers. Lipid identification does
  not rely on a database resource of reference or simulated mass spectra, but
  uses user-defined molecular fragment queries. It supports accurate,
  isotope-corrected quantification based on the identified MS1 or MS2 level
  fragments.
type: software
version: 1.5.0
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/lifs-tools/lipidxplorer"
url: "https://lifs-tools.org/lipidxplorer.html"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.3483976
keywords:
  - lipidomics
  - shotgun lipidomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - molecular fragmentation query language
  - lipid identification
  - lipid quantification
